# Scratch captured from provider APIs while working out chain detection, plus
# the throwaway scripts that captured it. They were raw API responses named after
# whatever chain was being probed (bt, bnb, bs, poly, rc1, rc56, rc137, tb, tt,
# tx, reth) and a couple of captured error bodies. Nothing reads them, they carry
# live timestamps rather than being reproducible fixtures, and at the repository
# root they read to anyone opening the project as unexplained data files.
# `_probe*.py` is covered too, so the next throwaway script does not land in git.
_probe*.py
/bt.json
/bnb.json
/bs.json
/poly.json
/bad2.json
/rc1.json
/rc56.json
/rc137.json
/reth.json
/tb.json
/tbb.json
/tt.json
/tx.json